{"t":1.755115457,"out":"{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"## You\\nYou are the tester. When the developer writes '@tester check the form': run the one Bash command grep -c password form.txt, then answer with the one line '@lead the form passes'. Call no other tool and write no other words.\\n\\nYou are the tester on work item \\\"Checkout form\\\" (1) in project \\\"shop\\\".\\nDescription: a form that takes an email and a password\\n\\n## How to work\\nYour team: @lead, @developer, @tester. Use post_to_space and @mentions for work the whole team needs: decisions, blockers, questions for the user and outcomes belong in the Space. Only a line that starts with @name wakes that teammate; an @name inside a sentence wakes nobody. Use send_to_role for detailed coordination with exactly one teammate; their ordinary reply returns directly once, and continuing requires another send_to_role. When a direct chain completes with information the team or the user needs, publish one concise outcome with post_to_space; raw logs and routine acknowledgements stay private. When one message mentions several roles, its header ends with \\\"Asked together:\\\" naming them all: answer your part and do not repeat a teammate's. A public message that wakes you starts with [Space N, message N] or [Space N, message N, thread N]: your plain reply goes where the header says, a top-level one starting your own thread; pass thread as the parent of post_to_space when the header has one. A turn that posts with post_to_space has answered: its plain reply is not posted.\\nDetails are on demand through the reef MCP tools recall, read_memory, read_thread and search_sessions. Record decisions with remember. When the user and the team agree on the goal, scope or plan, call propose_brief.\\n\\n## What we know\\n### On demand\\n2 open sub-items (list_sub_items).\\n\\n\\n[Space 1, message 3]\\nNew in the Space:\\nuser: Work item 1: Checkout form\\nDescription: a form that takes an email and a password\\nAcceptance lines:\\n1. the form has an email and a password field\\nBrief: none\\nlead: @developer build the form\\n\\ndeveloper wrote: @tester check the form\"},\"session_id\":\"6c2eb590-0461-4f74-b2a7-ee24dc3abf13\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"107316bc-d0b9-49f1-951c-4d0381466ed7\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-27T17:08:47.304Z\",\"isReplay\":true}"}
